:: Deadwood Raven Shrine Talk
<<effects>><<deadwood-raven-shrine-presence>>
<<if !_shrine or _shrine.stage isnot 3 or $location isnot 'forest_raven_shrine'>>
  <<lanSwitch 'You are no longer at the shrine.' '你已经不在神社了。'>><br><br>
  <<deadwood-raven-shrine-return>><<exit>>
<</if>>
<<if !_shrinePerson>>
  <<lanSwitch 'The veranda is empty. Tsukihan has other things to do; you can visit another time.' '廊下空着。月羽还有自己的事要忙，改天再来吧。'>><br><br>
  <<deadwood-raven-shrine-return>><<exit>>
<</if>>
<<set _shrineFirstMeeting to C.npc.Tsukihan.init isnot 1>>
<<npc Tsukihan>><<person1>>
<<if _shrineFirstMeeting>>
  <<language>>
    <<option 'EN'>>
      You hand over Gwylan's reply. Tsukihan takes it with a small bow and reads it through before speaking.<br><br>
      "Thank you. I will see to the rest." <<He>> folds it along the creases, keeping the edges even. A raven catches <<his>> sleeve in its beak. Tsukihan tugs the cloth free and smooths it down again.<br><br>
      "The courtyard is open to visitors. You may rest on the veranda, if you wish. The living quarters are private." <<He>> puts the letter away, then notices that the bird has left a feather on <<his>> sleeve. <<He>> brushes it off a little too quickly.
    <<option 'CN'>>
      你把格威岚的回信交过去。月羽微微颔首接下，看完以后才开口。<br><br>
      “多谢。余下的事，我来处理。”<<He>>沿原来的折痕收好信，仔细理齐纸边。一只渡鸦叼住了<<his>>袖口。月羽把布抽回来，重新抚平。<br><br>
      “庭院对来客开放。想歇脚的话，可以到廊下坐。屋舍是私人的，请留步。”<<He>>收起信，才发现袖子上还粘着根羽毛，抬手掸掉时稍微急了一点。
  <</language>><br><br>
<</if>>
<<if _shrine.scene is 'talk'>>
  <<switch _shrine.topic>>
    <<case 'shrine'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You ask who built the shrine. Tsukihan looks up at the red gate.
          "Someone who missed home, I think. The oldest papers are mostly accounts and lists of names. No grand revelation, I'm afraid."<br><br>
          <<He>> shows you a receipt for roof tiles. Someone has added a small bird in the margin.
          "I learnt the rites from the last person who cared for this place. Before anything else, they taught me where to put the buckets when it rains."
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你问起神社是谁建的。月羽抬头看了看红门。
          “大概是想家的人吧。留下来的旧纸，多是账目和人名。没找到什么惊天动地的秘密。”<br><br>
          <<He>>给你看一张买瓦的收据，页角还画着只小鸟。
          “祭仪是跟上一位照料这里的人学的。不过先学会的，是下雨时该把水桶放在哪儿。”
      <</language>>
    <<case 'birds'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You ask whether Tsukihan can tell the ravens apart. "Most of them. That one's missing a claw. That one opens bags. And that one waits for the others to open bags."<br><br>
          The last bird fluffs itself up. Tsukihan gives it a level look.
          "Yes, you. I watched you do it." <<He>> turns back to you. "They remember people who feed them. They remember people who throw things, too. I wouldn't try that."
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你问月羽能不能分清这些渡鸦。“大多认得。那只少一枚爪子，那只会拆袋子。还有那只，专等别的鸟拆开袋子。”<br><br>
          最后一只蓬起了毛。月羽看着它。
          “就是你。我亲眼看见的。”<<He>>转回头，“它们会记住喂过自己的人，也记得拿东西砸过它们的人。后面这件事就别试了。”
      <</language>>
    <<case 'town'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You tell Tsukihan about town. <<He>> listens while folding a shopping list into quarters.
          "I go down when we need supplies. Usually I get as far as the shop and remember three things I forgot to write down."<br><br>
          You notice biscuits at the bottom of the list. "For visitors," <<he>> says. Then, after a pause, "And me. They're rather good with tea."
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你说起镇上的事。月羽一边听，一边把采购单折成小小的一方。
          “缺东西时会下山。往往刚到店里，就想起还有三样没写上去。”<br><br>
          你瞥见单子最下面写着饼干。“给客人的。”<<he>>说，停了一下，又添上一句，“也给我自己。配茶挺好吃。”
      <</language>>
    <<case 'personal'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          <<if $speech_attitude is 'bratty'>>You glance at the tools and tease Tsukihan about spending even a quiet afternoon working.
          <<elseif $speech_attitude is 'meek'>>You tentatively ask what Tsukihan likes doing when there is no work to finish.
          <<else>>You ask what Tsukihan does with a quiet afternoon.<</if>><br><br>
          "I mend things. I read. Sometimes I start mending something and spend an hour looking for the tool I put down." Tsukihan pauses.
          <<if C.npc.Tsukihan.dom lt 30>>"Occasionally. The work does get done." <<He>> squares the cloth on <<his>> knee.
          <<else>><<He>> smiles at you. "Now you know. I always think I will remember where it is."<</if>><br><br>
          <<if isLoveInterest('Tsukihan') and C.npc.Tsukihan.love gte 20>>
            <<if C.npc.Tsukihan.dom gte 70>>
              <<He>> sets the cloth down. "Today, I want you to stay for a little while. Just because I have chores doesn't mean I only want help with them."
            <<elseif C.npc.Tsukihan.dom gte 30>>
              "Lately I keep looking up whenever I hear footsteps." <<He>> meets your eyes briefly. "I suppose you know why."
            <<else>>
              "There are usually spare cushions." <<He>> straightens the one beside <<him>>. "If you happen to come by."
            <</if>>
          <<elseif C.npc.Tsukihan.dom gte 70>>
            "Your turn. I can't always be the one finding something to talk about." <<He>> turns the cloth over, then looks up again, waiting for you to begin.
          <<else>>
            "What about you?" <<He>> waits for your answer, hands folded neatly on the cloth.
          <</if>>
        <<option 'CN'>>
          <<if $speech_attitude is 'bratty'>>你瞥了眼工具，打趣月羽，难得清闲下来也要找点活做。
          <<elseif $speech_attitude is 'meek'>>你小心地问起月羽不忙时的消遣。
          <<else>>你问月羽，清闲的下午一般怎么过。<</if>><br><br>
          “补补东西，看看书。有时东西没补上，倒花了一个钟头找刚放下的工具。”话一出口，月羽就顿了顿。
          <<if C.npc.Tsukihan.dom lt 30>>“只是偶尔。该做的事都有做完。”<<He>>把膝上的布叠得更整齐了些。
          <<else>><<He>>朝你笑了笑。“倒让你听见了。我放东西时明明都记得。”<</if>><br><br>
          <<if isLoveInterest('Tsukihan') and C.npc.Tsukihan.love gte 20>>
            <<if C.npc.Tsukihan.dom gte 70>>
              <<He>>把布放下。“今天想让你多陪一会儿。我这里有活干，又不是只想让你帮忙。”
            <<elseif C.npc.Tsukihan.dom gte 30>>
              “最近一听见脚步声，就会抬头看看。”<<He>>短暂地望进你的眼睛。“为什么，你应该猜得到吧。”
            <<else>>
              “廊下的坐垫，平时有空着的。”<<He>>理了理身旁那一只。“要是你恰好路过。”
            <</if>>
          <<elseif C.npc.Tsukihan.dom gte 70>>
            “轮到你了。总不能回回都由我找话说。”<<He>>把布翻过来，又抬眼看看你，等着你开口。
          <<else>>
            “你呢？”<<He>>把手整齐地放在布上，等着你的回答。
          <</if>>
      <</language>>
  <</switch>><br><br>
  <<if _shrine.step is ''>>
    <<socialiseicon 'ask'>><<lanLink ['Ask a little more', '再多问几句']>><<deadwood-raven-shrine-step 'ask' 'talk'>><</lanLink>><br>
    <<socialiseicon>><<lanLink ['Tell Tsukihan something about your day', '也说说你今天的事']>><<deadwood-raven-shrine-step 'tell' 'talk'>><</lanLink>><br>
    <<icon 'raven-shrine/bench.png'>><<lanLink ['Sit and listen for a while', '坐着听一会儿']>><<deadwood-raven-shrine-step 'listen' 'talk'>><</lanLink>><br>
    <<socialiseicon>><<lanLink ['Keep the conversation to shrine business', '只聊些神社的日常']>><<deadwood-raven-shrine-step 'formal' 'talk'>><</lanLink>><<deadwood-tsukihan-wilfulness-hint -1>><br>
  <<else>>
    <<switch _shrine.step>>
      <<case 'ask'>>
        <<if _shrine.topic is 'birds'>>
          <<lanSwitch 'You ask about the letter. "The birds carry things between places they know. Whether the right person gets them is another matter." Tsukihan points at a chewed cord. "We lost two lists before yours. Thank you for bringing it all the way."' '你问起那封信。“它们会把东西带到认识的地方。最后是不是到了该收信的人手里，就得另说了。”月羽指指被啄烂的细绳。“你那封之前，已经丢了两张清单。谢谢你特意送来。”'>>
        <<elseif _shrine.topic is 'shrine'>>
          <<lanSwitch 'You ask whether people still leave wishes. "They do. Some want someone to come home; others want the courage to leave." Tsukihan puts the old receipt away. "I keep their names to myself. You can leave yours unwritten, if you prefer."' '你问现在还有没有人来留下心愿。“有。有人盼着谁回家，也有人想有勇气离开。”月羽收起旧收据。“他们的名字，我就不讲了。你若想祈愿，也不必一定写下来。”'>>
        <<elseif _shrine.topic is 'personal'>>
          <<lanSwitch 'You ask what Tsukihan has been reading. <<He>> holds up a book with a scrap of cloth tucked between the pages. "Someone left it here. I meant to read a chapter, but it got dark before I noticed." <<He>> turns it over to show you the title. "You can borrow it when I finish. Tell me whether you think the ending will be any good."' '你问月羽最近在看什么书。<<He>>举起一本夹着碎布条的书。“有人落在这儿的。本来只想看一章，回过神来天都黑了。”<<He>>翻过封面，给你看书名。“等我看完，可以借你。先猜猜看，结尾会不会写得好。”'>>
        <<else>>
          <<lanSwitch 'Tsukihan answers your questions, then asks a few of <<his>> own. Before long, you have both forgotten the shopping list. "Now I\'ve thought of another thing to put on it," <<he>> says, reaching for a pencil.' '月羽回答了你的问题，也反过来问了几句。聊着聊着，两人都把采购单忘在了一旁。“这下又想起一件该买的了。”<<he>>说着，去拿铅笔。'>>
        <</if>>
      <<case 'tell'>>
        <<lanSwitch 'You tell Tsukihan what your day has been like. <<He>> sets <<his>> work aside and lets you finish. "Would you like advice, or would you rather I just listened?"' '你说起今天过得怎么样。月羽放下手里的东西，等你说完。“想听听我的意见，还是只想找个人说说？”'>><br><br>
        <<socialiseicon 'ask'>><<lanLink ['Ask what Tsukihan thinks', '想听听月羽的意见']>><<deadwood-raven-shrine-step 'advice' 'talk' '' 'tell'>><</lanLink>><br>
        <<socialiseicon>><<lanLink ['Just ask Tsukihan to listen', '只想让月羽听一听']>><<deadwood-raven-shrine-step 'listen_more' 'talk' '' 'tell'>><</lanLink>><br>
      <<case 'advice'>>
        <<lanSwitch 'Tsukihan thinks before answering. "I’d put off anything that can wait. Mind you, that’s how I ended up fixing six shutters in one afternoon." <<He>> looks ruefully towards the windows. "You can stay here a little longer, if it helps. I’ll try not to give you any more jobs."' '月羽想了想才开口。“我的话，能缓一缓的事，就先放着。虽说也正因为这样，有天下午一口气修了六扇窗。”<<He>>无奈地朝窗户看了一眼。“要是坐着舒服些，就再待会儿吧。我尽量不给你找活干。”'>>
      <<case 'listen_more'>>
        <<lanSwitch '"Then I\'ll listen." Tsukihan sets the cloth aside. <<He>> does not interrupt when you lose your place, or ask you to explain the parts you would rather leave alone. Eventually the words come a little more easily.' '“那我就听着。”月羽把布放到一旁。你说到一半卡住时，<<he>>没有打断。你不想细讲的地方，<<he>>也没有追问。后来，话渐渐好说了一些。'>>
      <<case 'formal'>>
        <<lanSwitch 'You keep the conversation on the shrine and its visitors. Tsukihan straightens the papers between you and answers in the same measured tone. When you leave a subject alone, <<he>> does too. Soon you are comparing which part of the path needs clearing next.' '你把话题留在神社和来客上。月羽理齐你们中间的纸张，用同样平稳的语调回答。你没再细问的事，<<he>>也没有提起。后来，你们说起了参道上下一处该清理的地方。'>>
      <<case 'listen'>>
        <<lanSwitch 'You let the conversation settle. Tsukihan returns to the cloth, occasionally showing you a crooked stitch or a loose thread. You do not have to answer every time. After a while, <<he>> puts it aside. "That was nice. We should do it again."' '你让话头慢慢停下来。月羽继续叠布，偶尔给你看看歪掉的针脚或松开的线头。你不必每次都接话。过了一会儿，<<he>>把布放下。“这样也挺好。下次再坐坐。”'>>
    <</switch>><<lstress>><<glove>><br><br>
    <<if _shrine.step isnot 'tell'>>
      <<getouticon>><<lanLink ['Finish talking', '结束交谈'] 'Deadwood Raven Shrine Talk'>>
        <<set $MoreTransformations.shrine.scene to '', $MoreTransformations.shrine.step to ''>>
      <</lanLink>><br>
    <</if>>
  <</if>>
<<elseif _shrine.talk is Math.floor(Time.days)>>
  <<lanSwitch 'Tsukihan picks up the unfinished cloth again. "I\'d better finish this before I lose the thread. Come and tell me the rest tomorrow."' '月羽重新拿起没收好的布。“趁还记得做到哪儿，先把它弄完吧。剩下的明天再说给我听。”'>><br><br>
<<elseif _shrineMinutes lte 10>>
  <<lanSwitch 'Tsukihan checks the fading light. "I\'m about to close up. I can say hello, but a proper chat will have to wait until tomorrow."' '月羽看了看渐暗的天色。“快要收拾关门了。打个招呼还行，细聊得等明天。”'>><br><br>
<<elseif $daily.no_sing or $worn.face.type.includes('gag')>>
  <<lanSwitch 'You cannot speak clearly. Tsukihan makes room for you to sit without pressing you for an answer.' '你说不清话。月羽给你腾出坐的位置，没有催着你回答。'>><br><br>
<<else>>
  <<lanSwitch 'Tsukihan folds the cloth onto <<his>> knee. "What is it?"' '月羽把布叠在膝上。“怎么了？”'>><br><br>
  <<for _topic, _label range { shrine: ['Ask about the shrine (0:10)', '问问神社的事 (0:10)'], birds: ['Ask about the ravens (0:10)', '聊聊这些渡鸦 (0:10)'], town: ['Talk about town (0:10)', '说说镇上的事 (0:10)'], personal: ['Ask about Tsukihan (0:10)', '多了解一些月羽 (0:10)'] }>>
    <<capture _topic _label>>
      <<socialiseicon 'ask'>><<lanLink _label>>
        <<deadwood-raven-shrine-act 'talk' _topic>><<if _shrineDone>><<goto 'Deadwood Raven Shrine Talk'>><</if>>
      <</lanLink>><<lstress>><<glove>><br>
    <</capture>>
  <</for>>
<</if>>
<br><<deadwood-raven-shrine-return 'veranda'>>
